# Both players' stocks in the debug VS match on Final Destination: Link
# (player 1) against a Mario who stands still with no input, three stocks
# each. Link dashes over and smashes Mario off the right edge: Mario's
# damage is said in the opponents' voice as the smashes land, then
# "2 stocks" on the tick he falls, with no label, as the match has one
# opponent. Link then walks off the left edge himself: "2 stocks" in your
# voice. About 30 seconds.
# Run from Git Bash with the debug match switches, muted, so the voices
# render and log their "plays" lines (run_level.py sets the switches):
#   MELEE_DEBUG_VS=1 MELEE_DEBUG_VS_STOCKS=3 \
#     python tools/a11y/drive.py --muted tools/a11y/match_stocks.drive

# Start on the title screen goes straight into the debug match.
wait "state 0 scene 0$"
press Start until "boot scene: state \d+ scene 2$"
wait 'cue opponent position start' 60
sleep 1

# A dash to the middle, then short dashes and forward smashes until Mario
# goes over the edge and falls past the bottom blast zone.
press Right 900
sleep 1
search 'voice opponents: "2 stocks"$' Right A+Right Right A+Right Right A+Right Right A+Right Right A+Right Right A+Right Right A+Right Right A+Right Right A+Right Right A+Right
wait 'voice opponents plays: "2 stocks" '

# Link walks off the left edge: his own stocks, in your voice.
sleep 5
press Left 8000
wait 'voice yours: "2 stocks"$' 30
wait 'voice yours plays: "2 stocks" '
sleep 1
